minimax-h3-mlx (https://github.com/PipeNetwork/minimax-h3-mlx)

The video VAE tile plan (runtime/video/h3/model/Geometry.cpp), the rotary tables
of install/video/convert_vae.py, the request preparation
(runtime/video/h3/model/Prep.mm) and the audio VAE decoder
(runtime/video/h3/ops/AudioDecoder.mm, install/video/convert_audio.py) follow
this MLX port of MiniMax H3, which the VAE converter also imports. Licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

BigVGAN (https://github.com/NVIDIA/BigVGAN)

MiniMax H3's audio VAE decoder is a BigVGAN generator; its kernels
(runtime/metal/kernels/video/audio) implement BigVGAN's anti-aliased
SnakeBeta activations and Kaiser-windowed sinc resampling. MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2024 NVIDIA CORPORATION, under the permission notice below.

MLX (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx)

The video request preparation (runtime/metal/kernels/video/prep,
runtime/video/h3/ops/PrepOps.mm, runtime/video/h3/model/Prep.mm) reproduces the
arithmetic of MLX 0.32.1's primitives, so that the prepared inputs equal
MLX's bit for bit: its GEMM and attention fragment orders, its GEMV, RMS norm
and sigmoid, and the threefry2x32 keys and erfinv polynomial of its
random.normal. No MLX code is linked or loaded.

TAEH3 / taehv (https://github.com/madebyollin/taehv)

The preview decoder runs the TAEH3 tiny decoder, whose weights the installer
downloads and install/video/convert_preview.py converts.

